          %h3#limits_and_colimits Limits and colimits
          %p
            Beware that, in general,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant presheaves
            need not be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
            set is always a sheaf:
          %p
          #TerminalSheaf.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (terminal sheaf)
              %br/
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              in its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{S})
              is, as a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
              with value the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+set"} singleton set
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Recalling the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
              of any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              into the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh(\mathcal{S})
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    PSh(\mathcal{S})
                    \\,,
            %p
              both functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserve
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              (this being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              over the
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+diagram"} empty diagram
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              because it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints+preserve+limits"} right adjoints preserve limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              because
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification+preserves+finite+limits"} sheafification preserves finite limits
            %p
              But the terminal presheaf is clearly the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} const
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \const_\ast \,\in\, PSh(\mathcal{S})
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant
              on the singleton set. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(const_\ast)
              is the terminal sheaf. But then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\big(L(const_\ast)\big)
              must again be the terminal presheaf, hence still the functor constant on the singleton set.
          %h3#EpiMonoIsomorphisms Epi- mono- and isomorphisms
          #RecognitionOfEpimorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+site"} small site
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C})
              be its category of sheaves. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              be a homomorphism of sheaves, hence a morphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C})
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  precisely if it is so
                  %em globally
                  in that for each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{C}
                  in the site, then the component
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi U
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_U \colon X(U) \to Y(U)
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
                  or
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  precisely if it is so
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em locally
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
                  and every element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y(U)
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p_i : U_i \to U\}_{i \in I}
                  such that for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
                  the element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(p_i)(y)
                  is in the image of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(U_i) : X(U_i) \to Y(U_i)
            %p
              But if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x_i\}_{i \in I}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points+of+a+topos"} points of a topos
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C})
              such that these are
              %em enough points
              (
              %a{:href => "point+of+a+topos#EnoughPoints"}> def.
              ) then the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is epi/mono/iso precisely it is is so an all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalks"} stalks
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x_i^\ast f \;\colon\; x_i^\ast X \longrightarrow x_i^\ast Y
            %p
              is a surjection/injection/bijection of sets, respectively, for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
