          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , vol 3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , sections A.4 and C.2 in
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
            %li#StacksProject
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
                ,
                %em Sites and sheaves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/download/sites.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The characterization of sheaf toposes and Grothendieck topologies in terms of left exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategories
            of a presheaf category is also in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p where it is implied by the combination of Corollary VII 4.7 and theorem V.4.1.
          %p
            There is also a direct proof in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shane+Kelly"} Shane Kelly
            %em What is the relationship between Grothendieck pretopologies and Grothendieck topologies?
            (
            %a{:href => "https://www.ms.u-tokyo.ac.jp/~kelly/pdfs/grothendieckTop.pdf"}> web
            ) .
          %p
            The characterization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S)
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
            with respect to local isomorphisms is emphasized at the beginning of the text
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              ,
              %em Stacks and non-abelian cohomology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.msri.org/publications/ln/msri/2002/introstacks/toen/1/index.html"}> web
              ) .
          %p Details are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
              (2006)
          %p It’s a bit odd that the full final statement does not seem to be stated there explicitly, but all the ingredients are discussed:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                exercise 16.7 shows that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
                inverts precisely the
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
                is an
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                lemma 16.3.2 states that the unit of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∘
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_{PSh(S)} \rightarrow i \circ \bar{(-)} : PSh(S) \to PSh(S)
                is componentwise a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
            %li
              %p
                using this corollary 7.2.2 says that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S) \simeq Ho_{PSh(S)}
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_{PSh(S)}
                formed using
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphism"} local isomorphism
          %p Letcure notes:
          %ul
            %li#Schapira23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"}> Pierre Schapira
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em An Introduction to Categories and Sheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~pierre.schapira/LectNotes/CatShv.pdf"} pdf
